# SHA-512 of every Guacamole artefact this installer will accept.
#
# This file is the pin. tools/vendor-guacamole.sh refuses to stage an artefact
# whose digest is not listed here, and install/lib/guacamole.sh refuses to
# deploy one — so a file dropped into this directory by hand, by a mirror, or
# by anything else has to match a hash that went through code review.
#
# Apache publishes a .sha256 beside each artefact; the vendor script checks
# that too. Two independent digests, one of them stored here rather than on the
# same host as the bytes it describes.
#
# Adding a version: run tools/vendor-guacamole.sh, which prints the line to add
# when it meets an artefact this file does not carry. Never edit a line to make
# a mismatch go away — a changed digest for a released Apache artefact means
# the bytes changed, and that needs explaining, not silencing.
#
# The .war and the -mysql .jar of the SAME version must be installed together;
# guacamole-ext is a version-locked API.

